	// ...
	htmlMeta, err := fetchHTMLMeta(url)
```

Delivery converges at **`httpgetter.GetHTMLMeta`**, which issues `httpClient.Get(urlStr)`:

```136:141:/bench/repo/internal/httpgetter/html_meta.go
func GetHTMLMeta(urlStr string) (*HTMLMeta, error) {
	if err := validateURL(urlStr); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}

	response, err := httpClient.Get(urlStr)
```

This is a separate delivery path from webhooks.

---

## What does **not** trigger outbound HTTP to user-configured URLs

| RPC / code | Why it is unrelated |
|---|---|
| `CreateUserWebhook`, `UpdateUserWebhook`, `ListUserWebhooks`, `DeleteUserWebhook`, `GetUserWebhookSigningSecret` | Only store/validate/reveal webhook config; no HTTP dispatch |
| `SignIn` (SSO) | HTTP to admin-configured IDP `UserInfoUrl` (`internal/idp/oauth2/oauth2.go:85`), not user webhook URLs |
| `Transcribe` | HTTP to instance AI provider endpoints (admin-configured) |
| `TestInstanceEmailSetting` | SMTP email, not HTTP to user URLs |
| SSE, OAuth tests, MCP adapter | Internal/test HTTP, not user-configured outbound delivery |

---

## Summary

| Category | RPC handlers (examples) | Convergence before HTTP delivery |
|---|---|---|
| **Persisted user webhook URLs** | `CreateMemo`, `UpdateMemo`, `DeleteMemo`, `CreateMemoComment`, `SetMemoAttachments`, `SetMemoRelations` | **`webhook.Post`** (`/bench/repo/internal/webhook/webhook.go:120`) via `webhook.PostAsync` |
| **Per-request user-supplied URLs** | `GetLinkMetadata`, `BatchGetLinkMetadata` | **`httpgetter.GetHTMLMeta`** (`/bench/repo/internal/httpgetter/html_meta.go:136`) |

For the webhook system specifically — the primary “user-configured URL” mechanism — the single delivery function is **`webhook.Post`**.

